Q1: Significance of HTTP Method Types.

Answer:
Method	Usage
GET	Retrieve a resource
POST	Create a new resource
PUT	Update an existing resource (full update)
DELETE	Delete a resource

These map directly to CRUD operations and are part of the HTTP specification.
Q2: RESTful resource naming guidelines.

Answer:

    Use plural nouns for resource names: /countries, /employees.

    Use hyphens for multi‑word resources: /menu-items.

    Append identifier for specific resource: /countries/{id}.

    Keep the URL consistent across methods for the same resource.

Method	URL	Description
GET	/countries	Get all
GET	/countries/{code}	Get one
POST	/countries	Create
PUT	/countries	Update
DELETE	/countries/{code}	Delete
